            <ArticleTitle>Acute coronary occlusion after recent coronary angioplasty. Association with exercise and successful treatment with intracoronary thrombolysis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>505-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of coronary occlusion occurred seven days after successful percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty. The acute complication occurred shortly after a negative exercise stress test and was resolved with intracoronary urokinase.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
